# ── Build output ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ESP-IDF (idf.py) is the single canonical build path.
build/

# ── Tool-generated sdkconfig ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# sdkconfig.defaults is the single tracked source of truth. Each toolchain
# regenerates its own concrete sdkconfig locally from it, so the generated
# variants stay out of git to stop one toolchain's config drifting against
# or overwriting the other's.
sdkconfig
sdkconfig.old
sdkconfig.esp32-s3-devkitc-1*

# ── Editor / tooling (local, not shared) ──────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/.browse.c_cpp.db*
.vscode/c_cpp_properties.json
.vscode/launch.json
.vscode/ipch
.clangd
.cache/
.claude/
__pycache__/

# ── Merged flash image (handover artifact, not source) ────────────────────────
# Produced by `esptool merge_bin` from build/ output. Regenerate per release
# rather than committing it: it is half a megabyte, changes every build, and
# under secure boot it is a SIGNED image — a stale copy in git is an easy way
# for someone to hand support the wrong firmware.
*-FULL.bin

# ── Per-release flash set (handover artifact, not source) ─────────────────────
# flash-set-<version>/ holds the compiled .bin images (bootloader, partition
# table, ota_data, app) plus SHA256SUMS, produced per release. The app image
# carries the MQTT broker credentials baked in as cleartext (no flash
# encryption), so it must NEVER land in git — a stale or leaked copy exposes the
# fleet password, and it bloats history (~0.5 MB/release). Hand the flash set
# over out of band or as a private release asset, not from the source tree.
flash-set-*/
*-flash-set.zip

# ── IDF Component Manager ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Fetched dependency sources (currently joltwallet/littlefs). Not committed —
# they are re-downloaded from the registry on build. NOTE: dependencies.lock IS
# committed deliberately, since it pins the exact versions and is what makes a
# rebuild reproducible.
managed_components/

# ── Scratch / generated artifacts (not source) ────────────────────────────────
# Wildcarded, not an exact filename: this dump is regenerated by hand and has
# been renamed once already (ALL_SOURCE_FOR_REVIEW.txt -> ..._SR.txt), which
# silently un-ignored a 350 KB generated file. The glob survives the next rename.
ALL_SOURCE_FOR_REVIEW*.txt

# ── Secure Boot signing key — NEVER COMMIT ────────────────────────────────────
# The RSA-3072 private key that signs every bootloader and app image. Anyone
# holding it can produce firmware that a secure-booted gateway will accept, so
# it is exactly as sensitive as the fleet itself. Losing it is equally bad in
# the other direction: eFuses are burned with its public-key digest, so without
# it those gateways can never be updated again.
#
# Keep it OUT of the repo entirely — offline, backed up, access-controlled.
# These patterns are a last-resort backstop against an accidental `git add .`,
# not the storage plan.
*.pem
secure_boot_signing_key*
*.key

# ── OS cruft ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ── Local flash helper (this machine only, not shared) ────────────────────────
# esptool timeout/retry overrides that work around this laptop's USB-Serial/JTAG
# write-timeout. Machine-specific, so it stays local rather than in the repo.
esptool.cfg
